\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N$, $\mathbb Z$, $\mathbb Q$, $\mathbb R$, and $\mathbb C$ denote the natural numbers, integers, rationals, reals, and complex numbers, respectively. All additional parameters and hypotheses are specified in the question.


\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For a graph with maximum degree $\Delta$ and clique number $\omega$, how many colors can be saved in ordinary, list, or correspondence coloring relative to bounds from $\Delta$, $\omega$, and maximum average degree; in particular, is the strong chromatic index at most $1.25\Delta^2$?
\par\smallskip\textit{Formulation references:} \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]}, \href{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2016/2}{[S2]}.

\subsection{Short English statement}
For a graph with maximum degree $\Delta$ and clique number $\omega$, how many colors can be saved in ordinary, list, or correspondence coloring relative to bounds from $\Delta$, $\omega$, and maximum average degree; in particular, is the strong chromatic index at most $1.25\Delta^2$?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] ULAM.AI and the UnsolvedMath Contributors, UnsolvedMath: A Curated Collection of Open Mathematics Problems, record 30003025 (OWR-14210-001). Catalogue attribution under CC BY 4.0.
\url{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}.
\item[S2] Original problem formulation and mathematical context.
\url{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2016/2}.
\end{itemize}
\label{end:30003025}

